# The hfcast-engine commit that this repository builds and tests against.
#
# The engine is a separate repository. Both workflows here clone it and
# check out this commit, so a build can be made again later and give the
# same binary. This file is the only place the value is written: it was
# in two workflows before, and they drifted apart.
#
# Move it deliberately. The evidence that a new commit is safe is the
# server test run: the server talks to the engine over a JSON contract
# through a subprocess, and nothing else checks that the two agree. Build
# the engine at the new commit and run `pnpm test` with HFCAST_PREDICT
# pointing at it. Say in the commit message what moved and why.
#
# Comments and blank space are removed when it is read. What is left must
# be one full 40-character commit hash.
